        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "For the first time, scientists have observed a star swallowing a planet. The amazing event took place in our "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Milky Way galaxy",
            "zh": "银河系"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", near the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Aquila constellation",
            "zh": "天鹰座"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". This location is about 12,000 light years away from our Earth."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In this new study, a team of scientists first noticed a strange star. Its brightness suddenly increased by more than 100 times over a ten-day period, which caught their attention."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The scientists looked further at the star through telescopes. They found it to be quite similar to our Sun in size and type. The star swallowed a planet over a period of about 100 days. The planet was a hot "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "gas giant",
            "zh": "气态巨行星"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Its "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "mass",
            "ref": "v-mass"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " was similar to that of "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Jupiter",
            "zh": "木星"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The planet was "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "orbiting",
            "ref": "v-orbit"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " very close to its star. It completed an entire orbit around the star in just one Earth day."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The star "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "nibbled at",
            "zh": "蚕食"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the planet’s edges as it began to swallow it slowly. In the final ten days, the rest of the planet fell inside the star completely. When the planet was totally destroyed, there was a bright "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "explosion",
            "ref": "v-explosion"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " that made the star shine brightly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "According to scientists, most planets will meet their end when their star runs out of energy and expands. Earth will meet a similar end when our Sun grows old—but not for another five billion years, so we don’t need to worry now."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
